From b39db88327ff24aabe2d27ebb8223d365dbf2614 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for konata09)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:57:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] clk: hisilicon: add Ascend 310 A55 cluster PLL driver

The Ascend 310 boot firmware programs the A55 cluster PLL (PLL5) to
1.6 GHz, and the kernel has no way to change the CPU clock. Add a clock
driver for the PLL so that its rate can be set from the device tree with
assigned-clock-rates.

The cluster has no clock mux to park on while the PLL is reprogrammed,
and powering the PLL down would stop every CPU. The rate is changed by
ramping the feedback multiplier in steps of 1/16 of the reference while
the PLL keeps running; it follows without losing lock.

PLL5 also feeds the SD/eMMC controller through its own dividers, so that
driver needs to know the rate and keep it fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
